- A1c is difficult to control (for example persistently >8–9%) despite primary care adjustments
- You’re on complex diabetes therapy (multiple daily insulin injections, frequent dose adjustments, or GLP-1/SGLT2 starting considerations)
- Recurrent hypoglycemia or symptomatic blood sugar variability
- Rapidly declining kidney function, significant albuminuria, or other complications that complicate diabetes meds
- Need for specialized evaluation (possible secondary diabetes, atypical presentation, or consideration of insulin pump/advanced therapies)
