- Beta-blockers (metoprolol) can blunt hypoglycemia symptoms (tremor/tachycardia) — important to consider when adjusting diabetes care.
- ACE inhibitor (lisinopril) is generally beneficial in diabetes and heart failure but requires kidney function and potassium monitoring when adjusting dose or adding drugs.
- Anticoagulation (apixaban) + uncontrolled hypertension: very high BP increases bleeding risk; better BP control reduces risk.
- Sleep apnea worsens BP control and insulin resistance — confirm CPAP adherence and effect on daytime symptoms.

